{{#is_alert}}The LLM Obs evaluation judges spent over $0.50 in the trailing 24h — ten times the current pipeline's rate. Either the judge is reading far more of each span than it did in the preview, the evaluation lost its service:webhook scope and is judging corpus runs, or a PR train landed. Check the evaluation's scope and sampling first.{{/is_alert}}
{{#is_warning}}The evaluation judges spent over $0.25 in the trailing 24h — five times the current rate; a glance, not a page.{{/is_warning}}

This is the judges' own spend (RC1-408), separate from the reviews' spend that the fleet guardrail watches. Datadog meters it as `ml_obs.estimated_usage.llm.evaluation.estimated_cost.nanodollars`, tagged by `evaluation_name` and the judge `model_name`; since 2026-09-12 the calls bill to Reid's Anthropic workspace `datadog-llm-obs-evals`, which carries its own monthly spend cap — this monitor is the early signal, the workspace cap is the hard stop.

Thresholds were set from the free preview (2026-09-02 to 09-12): the prompt-injection judge read ~1.3M tokens/day (~$1/day) while the retired single loop ran, and ~23k tokens/day (~2c/day) on the pipeline since 2026-09-07; $5.04 over the whole preview. Re-derive if a second evaluation is enabled or the judge model changes.

